{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1437142-planes-trains-and-automobiles","id":1437142,"title":"Planes, Trains, and Automobiles","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-02-26T13:10:32-08:00","id":1437142,"title":"Planes, Trains, and Automobiles","content":"The Ferrymen have been a favorite fixture of mine as far back as CWoD Wraith, and I love the idea of PC Ferrymen. I do love the archetype but I wonder if it can be flexible enough to work with other archetypes than sailing.<br /> <br /> Do the Rivers cut gouges so deep in the underworld that a plane or derigible could fly down it's course, buffeted by sinister storms and eyed by flying lovecraftian cthonians? Are there trains that plow down tracks of ankle deep (but still very dangerous) waters, or even taxi cabs? Are boats really the only way Ferrymen work? Are the phantom trains and ghost taxis relegated to the Surface World? <br /> <br /> Slightly related to it and inspired by the closed thread on the forum, are there Lakes and small Seas in the Rivvers, bordering several River Cities and potentially domains? Reaper pirates, large trade centers? Do they mechanically count as a River, just bigger?<br /> <br /> I ask because Gotham and Metropolis has a very urban underground and the boats don't always fit well. Sure, they're fine deeper in, and I've used them before, but it'd be interesting to see if those options are out of line or perfect doable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"